From: Onuralp SEZER <thunderbirdtr@fedoraproject.org>
Subject: [PATCH] continuous_batching: give BorrowedLinearAttentionRowsGuard a constructor

The guard declares (deleted) copy operations, so under C++20 it is no longer
an aggregate and `BorrowedLinearAttentionRowsGuard guard{*this, output};`
fails with "no matching function for call" (GCC 16 defaults to C++20).
Add the constructor the brace initialization expects.

--- a/src/cpp/src/continuous_batching/pipeline_impl.cpp
+++ b/src/cpp/src/continuous_batching/pipeline_impl.cpp
@@ -529,6 +529,9 @@
         const Scheduler::Output& m_scheduler_output;
         bool m_armed = true;
 
+        BorrowedLinearAttentionRowsGuard(ContinuousBatchingImpl& impl, const Scheduler::Output& scheduler_output)
+            : m_impl(impl),
+              m_scheduler_output(scheduler_output) {}
         ~BorrowedLinearAttentionRowsGuard() {
             if (m_armed) {
                 m_impl._release_linear_attention_borrowed_rows(m_scheduler_output);
